WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.230
- During my time at university,

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:03.510
I completed quite a few degrees.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.220
I started enrolling myself
in a bachelor of philosophy

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:09.450
with minors in history of
arts, and in economics.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.440
Next, I enrolled myself

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.010
in a bachelor of business administration,

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.760
both at the University of Munich, LMU.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.960
Actually completed this
one in five semesters,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.560
the bachelor philosophy in
the regular six semesters.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.430
During my bachelor
business administration,

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.430
I also spent a semester abroad

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.850
at Boccone University in Milan.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.860
Then during the middle of my bachelor,

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.060
I enrolled myself in the bachelor of laws,

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.850
at the Distance University Hagen,

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.300
and the later completed that as well.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.430
At the same time, I enrolled
myself at the CDTM program,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.710
which is a joint institution
of the TU Munich,

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.500
the Technical University
Munich, and the LMU, Munich.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.170
And I graduated with an honors degree

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.670
in technology management.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.330
I then later enrolled for a
master in accounting and finance

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.080
at London School of Economics.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.320
And then of course, in the end,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.760
I also completed my MBA at INSEAD.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:58.618
So in this video,

00:00:58.618 --> 00:01:00.140
I'm going to talk about exactly that,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.060
how did I do that?

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:01.893
How did I study?

00:01:01.893 --> 00:01:04.410
Three bachelor degrees in parallel?

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.990
And I will also share a couple of tips,

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.060
if you intend to do
something similar as well.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.990
And the last will reflect

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:13.560
whether this actually helped
myself in my career or not.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.180
So let's get out and let's get going.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.780
It's a beautiful weekend here in Munich.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.110
Today we're visiting
some of the Munich lakes.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.090
So let me share a couple of considerations

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.330
that you have in your mind

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.340
when thinking about
starting several bachelors

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:25.430
at the same time.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.610
The first is the selection
of the university.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.990
Here, especially some
private business schools

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.350
might not even offer
different degree programs.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.460
At many private business schools,

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.820
you can indeed only study business.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.480
The second limitation is that often

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.680
also the regulations of university

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.380
sometimes do not allow you to be enrolled

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.303
in several degree
programs at the same time.

00:01:45.303 --> 00:01:48.320
Here in Germany it's especially
the big public universities

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.270
that often are little bit more lenient.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.030
I studied at the University of Munich

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.327
for my first two bachelor degrees,

00:01:53.327 --> 00:01:55.400
and a third at Distance University.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.610
So make sure that the choice of university

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.900
supports the study programs
that you want to study.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.710
Second, make sure to combine subjects

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.210
that actually compatible with each other,

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.940
in regards to the examination
structure that they have.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.950
Here, one advantage of
pairing for instance,

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.050
a business degree with liberal arts,

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.100
is the business to use usually
are very heavy on exams.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.520
So at the end of the semester,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.580
you will usually have an exam period

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.210
where you'll have lots of exams.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:21.220
And on the other hand, for liberal arts,

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.440
there are usually almost no exams at all.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.150
That examination structure looks the way

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:27.050
that you will write lots of essays,

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.710
lots of written coursework
that you need to prepare.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.600
And these will often need to
be written during the semester.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.640
So I did the advantage that
at the end of the semester,

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.090
I was able to just study
for my business exams,

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.230
and didn't need to do that
much work during the semester

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:40.090
for this degree.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.340
And during the semester then,

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.300
I indeed had the time to focus
for the philosophy degree,

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.820
and make that work.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:49.240
Third thing strategically
about the semester abroad

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.073
that you might do.

00:02:50.073 --> 00:02:53.590
So I did a semester abroad at
Bocconi University in Milan

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.290
and that actually helped me

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.760
to finish my business degree earlier,

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.310
because I indeed finished
my bachelor in business

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:03.160
in five semesters,
instead of six semesters,

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.457
including the bachelor of theaters.

00:03:04.457 --> 00:03:06.160
And one of the main ways I did this

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.510
is that in Milan at Bocconi,
I wrote a full exam period

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:11.890
and I was able to carry
over many of the exams

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.550
that I wrote in Milan
towards my business degree.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.680
And then once I came back from Milan,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.790
I also completed a full exam period

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:21.260
in the same semester in Munich as well

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.950
because there the exams
happen a little bit later

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.740
than the exams in Milan
and still had time,

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.950
couple of weeks to
prepare for these exams.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.560
So pretty much did the
coursework of two semesters

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.393
in only one semester.

00:03:31.393 --> 00:03:33.590
And this one enabled me to, for instance

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:37.110
in my last semester complete
an internship at McKinsey.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:39.970
This enabled me then to fully
focus on my bachelor thesis

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:42.010
in philosophy in semester number six.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.870
Many students actually
extend their studies

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.400
if they do a semester abroad.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.470
In my experience if you
set it up the right way,

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.120
can actually help you
to complete your studies

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:50.953
in a quicker way.

00:03:50.953 --> 00:03:52.300
Let's now talk about time management

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.490
because this is a topic I
quite often your questions

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:55.930
on how did you manage to do all this?

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.380
How did you manage your time?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.040
In the past already created
a video about this topic.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.580
I will link it somewhere above here.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.570
Let me also know in the comments

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:04.550
if you would like to have
more content on that.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.470
I think the basic insight is

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.570
the time management in
these types of situations

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:10.270
isn't even that challenging.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:13.030
If you just have the
pressure that on this day

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.350
you will have the exam.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.900
You will make sure that
the day before the exams

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.170
you will do the study.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:19.340
If there was a coursework,

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.790
an essay that you need to submit,

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.720
you will make sure that in the days before

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.330
you will write this essay

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.750
because what would you do instead?

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:28.280
And the truth is most people
would just in the evenings

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.700
watch Netflix, hang out
maybe with some friends,

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.860
and so on, which of
course can also be fun.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.720
But personally, I found
that I can still do

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:35.553
lots of these things.

00:04:35.553 --> 00:04:37.660
I still have lots of fun,
was going out with friends,

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.270
but a couple of essay every semester,

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.270
a couple of exams in
the end of the semester,

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:42.760
this is still very much possible.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.830
If you just have the
deadline, the pressure,

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.290
and not just more or less forced

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.370
to put in the time to not fail.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:50.240
So was all the effort really worth it?

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.880
And let's look at that
from three perspectives.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.660
First to get my very first job,

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.060
in consulting at McKinsey.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.120
Second, for my mid to long
term career development.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.480
And third, just for my very personal life.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.580
First for McKinsey, did this
help me to get into McKinsey?

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:06.870
And very frankly I'd
say yes, it did help me.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.270
I think it was something a
little bit special that I did

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:12.220
to study both business philosophy, law.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.770
Surely not all the other
business candidates did that.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.580
I think especially when
you study business,

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.450
it's important to have a special spike,

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.090
something special that other people

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.500
are not necessarily doing.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.130
And for me, I'd say that
was one of the factors,

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.900
of course do not know how my
profile would've been assessed

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.260
if I wouldn't have done that,

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.200
but for sure that did not hurt me.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.940
Second, how did this help me with my roles

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:33.070
after McKinsey.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:35.020
And if frank, I didn't
think it had that much

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.260
of an effort more or
less all the things I did

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.670
after McKinsey were very much based

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.300
on my network, personal
relationships that I had

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.630
up to this job.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:46.020
Frankly I'm not sure if I will ever apply

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.870
to any job again in the future,

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:50.440
rather just classically
with a CV and a cold way

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:51.450
apply somewhere.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.620
And I think that's probably choice

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.790
independent from your degree.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.130
I think the further you
advance in your career,

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.830
the less important your
actually degrees will be

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.740
that you may be accomplished/attained
somewhere in the past.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.880
I think at some point it's just
not that important anymore.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.410
I think it especially helps you to get

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.180
into get that very first job.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.060
And third, how to assess this for myself,

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:11.260
for my personal development,

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.820
for the knowledge that I built.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.460
and here frankly starting
with the business degree

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:17.930
spanning a couple of years
in management consulting

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:19.980
would at least as effective

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.170
at starting completing
a bachelor in business.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:23.450
So that's why it helped me of course,

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.210
to get the context
understanding a couple of things

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.043
a bit better.

00:06:26.043 --> 00:06:28.330
Just for that probably the
time in consulting alone

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.720
would've done at least
that much for me myself.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.310
Second, the philosophy degree,

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:35.460
I think this very much shaped
just how I approach problems,

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.050
how I think about problems.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:38.930
I think it's just very
difficult also for myself

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:40.870
to see how I would approach things.

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:42.150
So I would see things

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:44.380
if I wouldn't have studied that degree.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.800
Surely it helped me a lot to
develop my critical thinking.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.670
It's very difficult for me to assess

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.800
how this would've looked like
if I wouldn't have done that.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.100
And thirdly law degree,

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.540
this might be actually the degree

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.810
where I got the most practical value from,

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:57.910
especially in my roles
after con consulting,

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.450
because directly after McKenzie,

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.710
I moved into a mid-size German retailer

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:04.180
in a restructuring role as a CTO.

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:06.810
And I was faced with
lots of legal questions

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:07.643
in this position.

00:07:07.643 --> 00:07:10.000
I did work together with
many lawyers at the time.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.890
Here this legal basic understanding

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:14.320
was insanely important helpful to me.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.070
And even now in my current role

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:18.620
in startup in the management
position in startup.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.270
I'm also facing legal
questions almost all the time.

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.240
And it's really important, helpful for me

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.840
to have this background.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.220
Of course, I'm not as
qualified as a lawyer,

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:29.160
but at least I know what
they're talking about.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.180
I can assess whether what someone tells me

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.500
makes sense or not.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.360
And this is immensely helpful indeed.

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:37.400
So if you study several degree
programs in parallel as well,

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.870
let me know about your
experiences in the comments.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:42.120
I do hope this may be inspired some of you

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.480
to do similar things
in the future as well.

